{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"SB0227","billNumberShort":"S.B. 227","billNumberLong":"SB0227S04","fileNumber":"2026FL1201","shortTitle":"Punitive Damages Amendments","currentSubVersion":"4","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"WINTER","primeSponsorName":"Sen. Winterton, Ronald M.","primeSponsorHouse":"S","floorSponsor":"JACKC","floorSponsorName":"Rep. Jack, Colin W.","floorSponsorHouse":"H","generalProvisions":"This bill enacts provisions relating to punitive damages.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>provides that an insurer may not rely on the existence, likelihood, possibility, or exposure to punitive damages when taking actions under Title 31A, Insurance Code;<hr><ltbullet>provides the circumstances in which a court may award punitive damages against an employer, managing agent, or principal for the conduct of the employer's, managing agent's, or principal's employee or agent;<hr><ltbullet>provides that the provisions this bill enacts apply only to a claim arising after the effective date of the bill; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Austin Weenig","fiscalAnalyst":"Gary R. Syphus","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/18/2026","trackingID":"WXJEHARDQV","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-30 09:52:58.727","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-30 09:52:58.740","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LLFA","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"LFA/ bill assigned to staff for fiscal analysis for SB0227","owner":"Legislative F